 this purpose, but no longer; see @(see sharp-dot-reader).)</p>

 <p>If you are at an ACL2 prompt (as opposed to a raw Lisp break), then you may
 type @(':a!') in place of @('(a!)'); see @(see keyword-commands).</p>

